=====================

so we can do this somewhat elegantly 
if we have a count_flops function
that is a copy of forward()
but then also returns a dictionary containing the flops

for names we can have each layer return: 'linear'
and the layer above can append attn.linear, then 0.attn.linear
and eventually we can build the right name without assigning any names.

it will break several of our layers though.
because we do stuff like: ln(ffn(x))

what if we count the number of flops during forward
then just use that number during count flops?
yeah I think that works best.

yeah so it really just is the number of parameters * the number of tokens for flops.
operational internsity is so low.

